[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A runner moves along a straight track at $4$ m/s.
An observer stands at $O$, a perpendicular distance of $8$ m from the track, and $P$ is the point of the track nearest to $O$.
When the runner is at $R$, let $x$ metres be the distance $PR$ and let $\theta$ be the angle $POR$, so that $\theta=\arctan\dfrac{x}{8}$.
Find the rate at which $\theta$ is increasing when $x=6$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (4,0);
\coordinate (R) at (4,2.4);
\draw (O) -- (P) node[midway, below] {$8$ m};
\draw[thick] (P) -- (R) node[midway, right] {$x$};
\draw (O) -- (R);
\draw[->] ($(R)+(0,0.25)$) -- ++(0,0.9) node[right] {$4$ m/s};
\draw ($(P)!0.3cm!(O)$) -- ($($(P)!0.3cm!(O)$)!0.3cm!90:(P)$) -- ($(P)!0.3cm!(R)$);
\pic[draw, angle radius=0.9cm, angle eccentricity=1.4, "$\theta$"] {angle=P--O--R};
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\node[below right] at (P) {$P$};
\node[right] at (R) {$R$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.question_text:
A picture $BT$ that is $3$ metres tall hangs on a wall so that its lower edge $B$ is $1$ metre above the eye $E$ of a viewer.
The viewer stands $x$ metres from the wall and $\theta$ is the angle the picture subtends at $E$.
a. Show that $\theta=\arctan\dfrac{4}{x}-\arctan\dfrac{1}{x}$.
b. Find the distance from the wall at which $\theta$ is greatest.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes,calc}
\coordinate (E) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3.2,0);
\coordinate (B) at (3.2,1);
\coordinate (T) at (3.2,4);
\draw (E) -- (P) node[midway, below] {$x$ m};
\draw (P) -- (B) node[midway, right] {$1$ m};
\draw[ultra thick] (B) -- (T) node[midway, right] {$3$ m};
\draw (E) -- (B);
\draw (E) -- (T);
\draw ($(P)!0.3cm!(E)$) -- ($($(P)!0.3cm!(E)$)!0.3cm!90:(P)$) -- ($(P)!0.3cm!(T)$);
\pic[draw, angle radius=1.3cm, angle eccentricity=1.35, "$\theta$"] {angle=B--E--T};
\node[below left] at (E) {$E$};
\node[below right] at (P) {$P$};
\node[left] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (T) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
